4o8|n|The act of arriving, or coming; the act of reaching a place from a distance, whether by water (as in its original sense) or by land. ; The attainment or reaching of any object, by effort, or in natural course; as, our arrival at this conclusion was wholly unexpected. ; The person or thing arriving or which has arrived; as, news brought by the last arrival. ; An approach.	n:267c,84,12;6vj,42,4;1ke,36,3~267c,84,12;6vj,42,4;1ke,36,3
